The published archive contains Cargo.toml, README.md, src/lib.rs and
src/test_utils.rs. All four are retained. The archive and upstream repository
omit a standalone license text. LICENSE-MIT supplies the standard MIT text
with author attribution from the manifest; it is not claimed to be a file
copied from upstream, and no copyright year has been inferred.

Local changes to src/lib.rs:
- Add a source attribution comment.
- Replace the uninhabited empty Class enum with an opaque #[repr(C)] struct
  containing a private zero-length byte array. Only pointers to Class cross
  the FFI boundary; the foreign symbol and pointer layout stay unchanged.
  This fixes the uninhabited_static lint (rust-lang/rust issue 74840).
- Make all default extern ABIs explicitly "C", preserving the previous ABI
  and fixing missing_abi warnings exposed for local path dependencies.
No warnings are suppressed. Cargo.toml, README.md and src/test_utils.rs are
byte-for-byte upstream. The public API and crate version are unchanged.

As checked during this patch, crates.io has no release newer than 0.1.6.
Upstream master revision 642ea4a4a5853a21b55b05c34832a5f1bb1af61c still
uses the uninhabited Class enum; switching to that revision does not fix it.

To verify original bytes and the exact permitted patch without executing
anything from the archive, run from the project root:
  python3 -I native/vendor/block-0.1.6/verify-source.py /path/to/block-0.1.6.crate
The verifier reads archive members without extracting them.
